{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1741","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Minimize the Thickness"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a sequence $$$a=[a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_n]$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positive"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call a group of consecutive elements a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is characterized by two indices: the index of its left end and the index of its right end. Denote by $$$a[l,r]$$$ a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the sequence $$$a$$$ with the left end in $$$l$$$ and the right end in $$$r$$$, i.e. $$$a[l,r]=[a_l, a_{l+1}, \\dots, a_r]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$a=[31,4,15,92,6,5]$$$, then $$$a[2,5]=[4,15,92,6]$$$, $$$a[5,5]=[6]$$$, $$$a[1,6]=[31,4,15,92,6,5]$$$ are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We split the given sequence $$$a$$$ into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" so that: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" each element is in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the sums of elements for all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"equal"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$a$$$ = [$$$55,45,30,30,40,100$$$], then such a sequence can be split into three "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": $$$a[1,2]=[55,45]$$$, $$$a[3,5]=[30, 30, 40]$$$, $$$a[6,6]=[100]$$$. Each element belongs to exactly "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", the sum of the elements of each "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is $$$100$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"thickness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of split as the length of the longest "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, the thickness of the split from the example above is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the minimum thickness among all possible splits of the given sequence of $$$a$$$ into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the required way."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case is described by two lines."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2000$$$) — the length of the sequence $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains exactly $$$n$$$ integers: $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^6$$$) — elements of the sequence $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ for all test cases does not exceed $$$2000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output one integer — the minimum possible thickness of a split of the sequence $$$a$$$ into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that there always exist a split, you can always consider whole sequence as one segment."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n6\n55 45 30 30 40 100\n4\n10 23 7 13\n5\n10 55 35 30 65\n6\n4 1 1 1 1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n4\n2\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The split in the first test case is explained in the statement, it can be shown that it is optimal."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, it is possible to split into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segments"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" only by leaving a single "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"segment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the thickness of this split is equal to the length of the entire sequence, that is, $$$4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the optimal split will be $$$[10, 55], [35, 30], [65]$$$. The thickness of the split equals to $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case possible splits are:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[4] + [1, 1, 1, 1] + [4]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$[4, 1, 1] + [1, 1, 4]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1741C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1741/problem/C"}